{
  "dom_id": "step-q101290",
  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "A sequence is defined as ${a}_{n}=2n+5$ for $n\\ge 1.$ What is the sum of the third and fourth terms?",
  "worked_solution": "We substitute $n=3$ and $n=4$ into the definition of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{3} & =2(3)+5=11 \\\\ {a}_{4} & =2(4)+5=13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the third and fourth terms is\n\n$$\n{a}_{3}+{a}_{4}=11+13=24.\n$$",
